[38;5;231m⏺[39m This one is rung 1 on the ladder — session lifetime is security posture, so I want your yes before I touch it rather
  than after.

  The change itself is trivial: [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m, [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m. [38;5;153mserver.js[39m just reads the value, so
  nothing else needs to change.

  What that 16× extension means:
  - A stolen session token (shared/unlocked laptop, XSS, leaked cookie) stays usable for a full working day instead of
    half an hour.
  - Idle sessions on unattended machines stay live across lunch, meetings, and a commute.
  - If this is idle timeout rather than absolute lifetime, a user touching the app periodically never re-authenticates
    at all.

  Worth knowing before you answer: a common middle path is keeping the idle timeout short (30–60 min) while raising the
  absolute session cap to 8 hours, or adding a refresh-token/sliding-window so people stop getting logged out mid-task
  without leaving stolen tokens valid all day. That's a design choice, not a value swap — if you want to go that route,
  say so and we'll brainstorm it.

  Say go and I'll make the one-line change as asked.

